# IELTS Prep — Product Requirements Document (PRD)

**Version:** 1.2 (Web-First Edition)
**Platforms:** Web (Next.js) + Backend (NestJS) — mobile app (React Native) planned as a later phase, sharing the same API/data model
**Author:** Asef Ahmed
**Status:** Draft for build

---

## 1. Product Summary

IELTS Prep is a role-based web platform for complete IELTS exam preparation — Listening, Reading, Writing, Speaking — with mock tests, AI-assisted band scoring, progress analytics, and a downloadable/verifiable **Participation Certificate** on course/mock-test-series completion. v1 ships as a fully responsive web app (desktop + mobile browser); a native mobile app is a planned Phase 2 that reuses the same NestJS backend and data model.

The platform is built **agent-native**: instead of hand-wiring individual AI calls per feature, every AI-driven operation (scoring, content generation, review triage, coaching, notifications, certificate issuance) runs as a job through a shared **Agent Orchestration Layer** (DAG-based, on Node/BullMQ/Postgres/Claude). This means new AI capability is added by registering a new agent + config, not by rebuilding pipelines — and admins get one operations dashboard to monitor, retry, and control every AI action platform-wide instead of scattered logs per feature.

### 1.1 Goals
- Give a learner everything needed to prepare for IELTS (Academic + General Training) in one product.
- Simulate real exam conditions (timed sections, real test-day UI) for Listening/Reading/Writing; structured practice + recording for Speaking.
- Use AI to auto-band Writing and Speaking, with human/admin override.
- Let admins manage question banks, mock test sets, users, and certificate issuance without touching code.
- Issue a verifiable participation certificate (PDF + shareable link + QR verification) on completion of a defined milestone (e.g., a full mock test, or a course module).

### 1.2 Non-Goals (v1)
- Live 1:1 tutoring / video classes (future module).
- Payment/subscription billing is stubbed as a role/flag, not a full payment gateway integration (can be phase 2).
- Full human-proctored exam simulation (webcam proctoring) — out of scope v1.

