## 3. Core Modules & Features

### 3.1 Authentication & Onboarding
- Email/password + Google/Apple OAuth.
- Email verification (OTP or magic link).
- Forgot/reset password.
- Onboarding wizard: target band score, exam date, module (Academic/General), current level (self-assessed or diagnostic quiz).
- Role assignment: default `student`; admins created via seed/invite only.

### 3.2 Dashboard (Student)
- Overall band prediction (average of latest section scores).
- Section-wise progress rings: Listening / Reading / Writing / Speaking.
- Study streak, daily goal tracker.
- Upcoming: recommended next test/lesson based on weakest section.
- Certificate status widget ("2 of 4 milestones complete").

### 3.3 Listening Module
- Full mock tests (4 sections, audio player, real exam timer ~30 min + 10 min transfer).
- Question types: MCQ, matching, form/note/table completion, map labeling, sentence completion.
- Auto-graded on submit; instant band-equivalent score + answer review with audio timestamp replay.

### 3.4 Reading Module
- Academic & General Training passage sets (3 passages, 60 min timer).
- Question types: TFNG/YNNG, matching headings, MCQ, summary completion, matching information.
- Auto-graded; review mode highlights passage evidence for each answer.

### 3.5 Writing Module
- Task 1 (Academic: chart/graph/process/map; General: letter) + Task 2 (essay).
- Rich text editor with live word count + timer (20/40 min).
- **AI scoring**, run by the **Writing Scoring Agent** (via Claude API), against the 4 official criteria: Task Achievement/Response, Coherence & Cohesion, Lexical Resource, Grammatical Range & Accuracy — returns band per criterion + overall + inline improvement comments + a confidence score.
- Low-confidence results are auto-routed by the agent orchestrator to the human review queue (no manual triage needed); high-confidence results publish straight to the student.
- Optional instructor review queue to confirm/override AI band.

### 3.6 Speaking Module
- Part 1/2/3 structured prompts with cue cards.
- In-browser audio recording via the MediaRecorder API (works on desktop and mobile browsers, no app install needed).
- AI transcription + band scoring (Fluency & Coherence, Lexical Resource, Grammatical Range, Pronunciation), run as a 2-step agent chain: **Transcription Agent** (STT) → **Speaking Scoring Agent** (Claude API), coordinated by the orchestrator so a failed step auto-retries without losing the recording.
- Playback with band feedback overlay; instructor override supported.

### 3.7 Practice Bank (non-timed)
- Topic-wise and difficulty-wise question drilling for all 4 skills.
- Bookmark/flag questions, personal notes.
- Vocabulary builder: word lists tied to reading/listening passages, spaced-repetition flashcards.

### 3.8 Mock Test Engine (generic, config-driven)
- Admin composes a "Test Set" from the question bank (pick sections, time limits, question order).
- Same engine powers Listening/Reading/Writing exactly as real IELTS test-day structure; supports a **Full Mock Test** (all 4 skills back-to-back) and **Section-only** mocks.
- Auto-calculates overall band score (average of 4, IELTS rounding rules).

### 3.9 Certificates
- **Participation Certificate** auto-generated on: completing N full mock tests (config, default 1) OR a defined course/module.
- Certificate contains: learner name, date, overall band achieved, unique certificate ID, QR code.
- PDF generation (server-side, templated, admin-editable template/branding).
- Public verification page: `/verify/:certificateId` — anyone can confirm authenticity without login.
- Student can download PDF, get a shareable link, or push to LinkedIn.
- Admin can view/revoke/reissue certificates.

### 3.10 AI Agent Platform Layer (cross-cutting)

Every AI-driven operation in the product is a registered **Agent** running through one shared orchestrator, not a one-off API call buried in a feature. This is what makes the platform "fully operable" — one place to see, monitor, retry, and extend every automated action.

**Core agents (v1):**

| Agent | Trigger | Job |
|---|---|---|
| **Writing Scoring Agent** | Writing submission | Bands the essay against the 4 IELTS criteria, returns confidence + feedback |
| **Speaking Scoring Agent** | Recording submitted + transcribed | Bands speaking against the 4 criteria |
| **Transcription Agent** | Speaking recording uploaded | STT → clean transcript, feeds Speaking Scoring Agent |
| **Content Generation Agent** | Admin requests "generate draft set" | Drafts new Reading passages/questions, Listening scripts, Writing/Speaking prompts from a topic + difficulty spec, for admin to review/edit/publish (never auto-publishes) |
| **Review Triage Agent** | Any AI score returned | Routes low-confidence or rubric-edge-case scores to the human review queue; auto-publishes high-confidence ones |
| **Coach Agent** | Nightly / on-demand per student | Reads a student's attempt history, produces the "recommended next action" + personalized weak-area practice set on the dashboard |
| **Certificate Agent** | Milestone met | Generates the PDF, QR code, verification record; notifies the student |
| **Notification Agent** | Various (score ready, streak, exam-date countdown) | Composes and dispatches push/email copy per event, personalized to the student |
| **Ops/Support Agent** (admin-facing) | Admin query in Admin panel | Natural-language ops queries — "which questions have the highest miss rate this month," "list students who stalled mid-mock this week" — answered by querying the platform data via tool calls, no SQL needed |

**How it works:**
- Each agent = a config (prompt/rubric, input schema, output schema, retry policy, confidence threshold) + a DAG node. Orchestrator (Node/BullMQ/Postgres/Claude) runs agents as background jobs, in parallel where independent (e.g., Writing + Speaking scoring for a full mock run concurrently) and in sequence where dependent (Transcription → Speaking Scoring).
- **Human-in-the-loop by default** for anything that reaches a student's grade or gets published as content — agents draft/score/suggest, admins/instructors approve or the confidence gate auto-publishes.
- Every agent run is logged: input, output, confidence, duration, retries, cost — visible in the Admin Agent Ops Dashboard (§3.11).
- Adding a new AI capability later (e.g., an "Interview Simulation Agent") means registering a new node in the same framework — no new pipeline, no new infra.
- This layer reuses the same generic agent-orchestration architecture already used across other products (Node/BullMQ/Postgres/Claude), so it's a known, provable pattern rather than a new build.

### 3.11 Analytics & Reporting
- Student: band trend chart over time, section strength/weakness radar chart, time spent per module.
- Admin: platform-wide usage, test attempt volume, average bands, drop-off points, content performance (which questions are most missed), certificate issuance log.

### 3.12 Admin Panel
- **Agent Ops Dashboard** — live view of every agent run (queued/running/done/failed), per-agent success rate, avg confidence, avg cost/latency, one-click retry or manual override on any failed/low-confidence run. This is the single control surface for "is the AI actually working" across the whole product.
- User management (search, view profile, role change, suspend/delete, impersonate-for-support).
- Content management: CRUD for passages, audio files, question sets, writing/speaking prompts, test sets; "Generate draft with AI" button (invokes Content Generation Agent) on every content type.
- Certificate template management.
- Review queue for AI-scored Writing/Speaking flagged as low-confidence (fed by the Review Triage Agent).
- Ops/Support Agent chat panel for natural-language platform queries.
- Global settings: band-rounding rules, certificate issuance rules, feature flags, per-agent confidence thresholds and retry policy.
- Audit log of all admin and agent actions.

### 3.13 Notifications
- Browser push + email, composed by the Notification Agent: test reminders, streak reminders, exam-date countdown, certificate ready, instructor feedback ready.
- In-app notification center.

### 3.14 Subscription / Access Tiers (stubbed for v1, real gateway in v2)
- Free tier: limited practice questions, 1 mock test/month.
- Premium: unlimited mocks, AI Writing/Speaking scoring, certificate eligibility.
- Admin can manually grant/override tier per user (for v1 without live payments).

