```

- **Backend:** NestJS, Prisma + PostgreSQL, Redis + BullMQ for async jobs, S3-compatible storage for audio uploads and generated certificate PDFs.
- **Agent Orchestration Layer:** a DAG-based engine (Node/BullMQ/Postgres/Claude) sitting behind the NestJS API. Every AI action in the product — scoring, content drafting, review triage, coaching recommendations, certificate generation, notification copy, admin ops queries — runs as a config-registered agent job through this one layer, with shared logging, retries, confidence gating, and cost tracking. This is the same generic agent-orchestration pattern used elsewhere, reapplied here rather than rebuilt per feature.
- **Web:** Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, fully responsive (desktop + mobile browser) — this is the entire v1 client surface, including test-taking, admin, and public/verify pages, SSR for public/marketing + verify pages, CSR for authenticated app.
- **Mobile (Phase 2, not in v1 scope):** React Native (Expo) app consuming the same NestJS API and shared types package once the web platform is stable.
- **AI:** Anthropic Claude API powers every agent; a speech-to-text vendor feeds the Transcription Agent.
- **Auth:** JWT access + refresh tokens, role claims, NestJS Guards; same auth service ready to be consumed by a future mobile client without backend changes.

