## 8. Non-Functional Requirements
- **Performance:** audio streaming must start <1s; test timer must be authoritative server-side (prevent client clock tampering).
- **Reliability:** in-progress attempts autosave to the server every 15–30s regardless of trigger (tab close, refresh, connection drop); resume-on-reconnect picks the attempt back up mid-test. A service worker can cache the current question set so a brief connectivity blip doesn't lose in-progress answers.
- **Security:** role-based guards on every API route; signed URLs for audio/certificate PDFs; rate-limiting on auth endpoints.
- **Scalability:** AI scoring and PDF/certificate generation run as background jobs (BullMQ) so API stays responsive under load.
- **Accessibility:** captions/transcripts available for listening audio (post-attempt), scalable font sizes, keyboard navigation.

